I don't understand exactly what are you suggesting. The exposed path is a list, could be several exposed paths. Labels should be different for each item on the list, right? Also, the documentation doesn't mention anything, but the code [checks for duplicates](https://github.com/hashicorp/consul/blob/master/agent/structs/structs.go#L1138-L1171). I thought about setting the labels as `__meta_consul_proxy_exposed_path_port_<path> = <port>`

For example, in the case of the following information for the service in consul:

```
{
  "expose": {
    "paths": [
      {
        "path": "/healthz",
        "local_path_port": 8080,
        "listener_port": 21500
      },
      {
        "path": "/metrics",
        "local_path_port": 8080,
        "listener_port": 21501
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

The following labels would be generated:

```
__meta_consul_proxy_exposed_path_port_healthz = 21500
__meta_consul_proxy_exposed_path_local_port_healthz = 8080
__meta_consul_proxy_exposed_path_port_metrics = 21501
__meta_consul_proxy_exposed_path_local_port_metrics = 8080
```

That way a relabel config could be done changing the `__address__` to the ip and port using `__meta_consul_proxy_exposed_path_port_metrics` where the metrics are exposed (supossing that you know your applications will expose the _/metrics_ path).

